  "about": "The gzip-9 parity's cases (spec 004 T064; contracts/plain-model-fit.md §7), which apps/web/test/room/gzip.test.ts checks through pako and scripts/assets/test_gzip_parity.py through Python's gzip.compress(data, 9, mtime=0). A case's bytes come from xorshift32 started at its seed: on 32 bits, x ^= x << 13, x ^= x >>> 17, x ^= x << 5, and each step's x is the next value. A draw from [lo, hi] is lo + (the next value mod (hi - lo + 1)); n random bytes are the next ceil(n / 4) values, each little-endian, the last cut short. First the pool: pool patterns, each of random bytes, its length drawn from period. Then rounds until the case holds its bytes: a run of random bytes, its length drawn from random; then, where pool isn't 0, a pattern drawn by its index from [0, pool - 1], repeated from its start to a run whose length is drawn from pattern. The whole is cut at bytes. crc32 is the bytes' CRC-32, and gzip9 their length after Python's gzip.compress(data, 9, mtime=0).",
